Don't remove a suffix from a root in basename on Windows.
POSIX basename leaves a path of slashes as "/" and skips the suffix
step for it. On Windows the result can also be a drive root or a UNC
root, which basename printed whole but then stripped of a matching
suffix: "basename C:/ /" printed "C:" and "basename //host/share re"
printed "//host/sha". Leave the suffix on a result that is a root,
which is the only kind of result to contain a separator or a drive.

---
 coreutils/basename.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/coreutils/basename.c
+++ b/coreutils/basename.c
@@ -74,7 +74,9 @@
 					bb_show_usage();
 			}
 		}
-		if (suffix) {
+		/* a root such as C:/ or //host/share keeps its suffix, as / does */
+		if (suffix IF_PLATFORM_MINGW32(&& !has_dos_drive_prefix(s)
+				&& !strpbrk(s, "/\\"))) {
 			size_t n = strlen(suffix);
 			if ((m > n) && (strcmp(s + m - n, suffix) == 0)) {
 				m -= n;
